<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gautamiputra Satakarni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gautamiputra Satakarni was a king of the Satavahana dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> in the early 2nd century CE. His mother's inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nashik">Nashik</a> credits him with defeating the Western Kshatrapa ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahapana">Nahapana</a> and restoring Satavahana power. His name, taken from his mother Gautami, reflects the dynasty's custom of naming kings after their mothers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gautamiputra-satakarni.jpg" alt="Gautamiputra Satakarni" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rapson, E. J. (Edward James), 1861-1937 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coinage_of_Gautamiputra_Satakarni_with_Brahmi_legend.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
